FILE: vUX-modalDisplayer.js
FEATURE: component-teardown
DATE: 2026-09-17
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'resizer-docs'

REASON
Two levels of listener here. The per-instance trigger listener was an anonymous document
'click' closure, so an instance could never stop responding to its own trigger class.
It is now the named handleTriggerClick.

The four document-level handlers (Escape, effect transitions, resize, away/close clicks)
are deliberately shared by every instance — binding them per instance would pop one layer
per instance for a single Escape press. They were attached once and never detached, so
they stayed bound even after every displayer on the page had been torn down. Initialized
instances are now counted, and the last one to be destroyed detaches them.

destroy() closes only the layers whose owner is this instance, walking the stack backwards
because completeClose() splices from it.

